  "name": "Nhạc tiền chiến (pre-1954 Vietnamese romantic song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The first generation of Vietnamese tân nhạc (new music), composed from the late 1930s to the early 1950s by writers such as Đặng Thế Phong, Văn Cao and Đoàn Chuẩn, setting Vietnamese lyric poetry to Western-style melody and harmony in verse-and-refrain forms. After 1954 the repertoire was kept alive chiefly in Saigon, where singers recorded it for radio and records with guitar, piano and small studio orchestras.",
  "recipe": "classic Asian nhạc tiền chiến, functional Song, east Asian pop branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. classical nylon-string guitar, grand piano. live tracking. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, broadcast loudness EQ. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
